<dl>
    <dt><strong>Answer</strong></dt>
    <dd>
    <p class="lt-chem-408787">To know which element was used as the sample, find the lattice parameter (a) using the equation for interplanar spacing \(\left(d_{h k l}\right)\), Bragg's law, and Moseley's law. For \(\mathrm{h,k,l}\) and \(\theta_{h k l}\), pick a plane and a corresponding angle from the chart we developed last chapter, shown below:</p>

