    \lambda=2 d_{h k l} \sin \left(\theta_{h k l}\right)<br />
    \end{gathered}</p>

    <p class="lt-chem-408787">The energy corresponds to \(\mathrm{Cu}(\mathrm{Z}=29) k_\alpha\)&nbsp;radiation:</p>

    <p class="lt-chem-408787">\begin{gathered}<br />
    E=\dfrac{h c}{\lambda}=13.6[e V](Z-1)^2\left(\dfrac{1}{n_f^2}-\dfrac{1}{n_i^2}\right) \\<br />
    \lambda=\dfrac{h c}{-13.6(Z-1)^2\left(\frac{1}{n_f^2}-\frac{1}{n_i^2}\right)} \\<br />
    d_{h k l}=\dfrac{h c}{-13.6(Z-1)^2\left(\frac{1}{n_f^2}-\frac{1}{n_i^2}\right) 2 \sin \theta_{h k l}} \\<br />
    a=\dfrac{h c \sqrt{h^2+k^2+l^2}}{-13.6(Z-1)^2\left(\frac{1}{n_f^2}-\frac{1}{n_i^2}\right) 2 \sin \theta_{h k l}}=3.53 A<br />
    \end{gathered}</p>

    <p class="lt-chem-408787">This lattice parameter corresponds to \(\mathrm{Ni}\).</p>
    </dd>
</dl>

